  "challenge": {
    "title": "Meeting Family Over a Meal",
    "instructions": "Write and say a short Iraqi conversation that lasts at least 10 lines. It must include a question about someone's family, a description of at least one relative, a statement of hunger or thirst, ordering or offering food and drink, the fixed exchange بالعافية / الله يعافيك or صحة وعافية / الله يسلمك, and asking for the bill. Use at least 8 target phrases from Unit 2 and include both a masculine-address form and a feminine-address form.",
    "required_elements": [
      "A question about family using عندك عايلة؟ or شكد واحد بعايلتك؟",
      "A description of at least one family member using أمي, أبوي, أخوي, أختي, زوجي, مرتي, ابني, or بنتي.",
      "A statement of hunger or thirst using جوعان, جوعانة, or عطشان.",
      "An order or offer of food or drink using أريد آكل or أريد أشرب.",
      "The fixed exchange بالعافية / الله يعافيك, or صحة وعافية / الله يسلمك.",
      "A request for the bill using الحساب لو سمحت or شكد الحساب؟",
      "Both a masculine-address form (such as عندك) and a feminine-address form (such as عندچ)."
    ],
    "model": {
      "dialogue": [
        {
